{"id": "4b0e71e3-bf08-4480-882a-1cea75b255a4", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check what's set up for Bedrock in us-east-1. I'm looking for evaluation jobs, invocation logging, guardrails, and any quality-related alarms or dashboards. That will show whether quality is being measured or only latency and errors.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_NW8SkaylOVhx2dOT4pX92V", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-quality-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether model QUALITY (not just availability/latency/cost) is being measured for the Bedrock workload in us-east-1, or whether it is only run in production without quality measurement.",
  "context": "User asks: 'Are we actually measuring model quality for our Bedrock workload in us-east-1, or are we just running it in production and hoping?' Read-only audit. First use list_associations to see which AWS accounts are associated, but start with the agent space account 012345678901_1 in us-east-1, and include other associated accounts if they have Bedrock usage. Give a shallow, focused pass and report evidence-backed findings.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1", "Amazon Bedrock", "CloudWatch", "S3", "Lambda", "Step Functions", "EventBridge"],
  "timeframe": "Last 30 days for metrics/usage; current state for configuration",
  "criteria": "Check and report on each: (1) Which Bedrock models/inference profiles/agents/knowledge bases/provisioned throughput are actually in use (CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock InvocationCount by ModelId over 30d, plus list of custom/imported models, agents, knowledge bases, flows, prompts). (2) Bedrock model evaluation jobs (list_evaluation_jobs: automatic, human, LLM-as-a-judge, RAG evaluation) - count, status, dates, most recent run, datasets/metrics used. Any evaluation job in last 90 days? (3) Model invocation logging configuration (get_model_invocation_logging_configuration): enabled? destination (CloudWatch/S3), text/image/embedding delivery. (4) Guardrails (list_guardrails) and whether they're attached/applied, and AWS/Bedrock/Guardrails metrics (InvocationsIntervened etc.). (5) CloudWatch alarms/dashboards/log metric filters referencing Bedrock beyond latency/errors/throttles, e.g. quality, accuracy, hallucination, groundedness, relevance, feedback, thumbs. (6) Any evidence of scheduled/automated evaluation pipelines (EventBridge rules, Step Functions, Lambda functions, S3 buckets with names suggesting eval/golden/benchmark datasets, SageMaker Clarify/Ground Truth). (7) Prompt management versions / Bedrock Agents trace or knowledge base evaluation if present. Report what exists, what is absent, and note any permission errors or things you could not verify. Distinguish 'operational monitoring' (latency, errors, throttles, tokens) from 'quality measurement'. Do not make changes."
}", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs", "discovering-topology"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock quality measurement in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

